{"id":"interim-certifications","tier":"OFFICIAL","title":"State list: negative and qualified certifications","question":"In which interim reports did the State list San Francisco Unified among districts that may not meet their obligations?","finding":"Of 22 interim reports from 2015-16 to 2025-26, the State listed the district 3 times with a negative certification (may not meet its obligations this year or next) and 5 times with a qualified one (may not meet them in the following three years). The negative run: 2023-24 second, 2024-25 first, 2024-25 second. In the two years of the payroll breakdown and the audit without an opinion (2021-22 and 2022-23) the district was not listed: it certified itself positive in all 4 reports.","how":"Each State status page (printed to PDF) lists negative and then qualified certifications; the district's line is placed by whether it falls before or after the \"Qualified Certification\" heading.","limits":"A certification is the district's own, reviewed by the county office; in San Francisco the county office is run by the same superintendent and board, and its review of the district's reports is signed by the district superintendent (Form CA, 2025-26). Not being listed means a positive certification, which the State team's later reviews did not share. In May 2024 the State changed the 2023-24 second interim rating from qualified to negative. The December 7 draft of the 2024-25 first interim ticked qualified. The final December 10 board copy ticked negative, matching the State list.","columns":[{"k":"year","t":"Fiscal year","type":"text"},{"k":"interim","t":"Report","type":"text"},{"k":"district","t":"School district","type":"text"},{"k":"budget","t":"Budget listed ($ millions)","type":"int"},{"k":"county","t":"County office","type":"text"},{"k":"doc","t":"State list","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"year":"2015-16","interim":"First","district":"Not listed (positive)","budget":null,"county":"Not listed (positive)","doc":{"t":"CDE first inte